(2543896, 345114, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2</b> <br/> <br/>Hi Margie. Let me first say I like the crop. I think that helps make the shot more interesting and eliminates any other distractions that may have been present. The problem I have with this shot is what Rebecca mentioned. It feels incomplete. I do like the bubbles which are over the top and perfect for this challenge but beyond that I feel the rest is lacking. I also don''t like seeing the back of your head which kinda looks like its an inanimate object as if it''s just hair sitting on top of a stereofoam head. Maybe show a bit of your profile and neck so it feels more real. Lastly, I feel the focus is too much on the candles, IMO. The candles situated in that dark corner has a lot of contrast and therefore my eyes pull to that instead of you.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-23 03:08:42.</i></td>', 'Greetings from CTP2  Hi Margie. Let me first say I like the crop. I think that helps make the shot more interesting and eliminates any other distractions that may have been present. The problem I have with this shot is what Rebecca mentioned. It feels incomplete. I do like the bubbles which are over the top and perfect for this challenge but beyond that I feel the rest is lacking. I also don''t like seeing the back of your head which kinda looks like its an inanimate object as if it''s just hair sitting on top of a stereofoam head. Maybe show a bit of your profile and neck so it feels more real. Lastly, I feel the focus is too much on the candles, IMO. The candles situated in that dark corner has a lot of contrast and therefore my eyes pull to that instead of you.', '2006-06-23 04:07:17.000000', '2006-06-23 04:08:42.000000', 0),
(2543918, 347522, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2</b> <br/> <br/>Let me first say this should have scored higher. You may be right about why it didn''t score higher but it could also be the neatimage, IMO. In any case it was a good entry. What I especially liked about this was the lighting and also the texture. The image also has a good tonal range and the whites and blacks are perfect. All in all a very good technical image that met the challenge.</td>', 'Greetings from CTP2  Let me first say this should have scored higher. You may be right about why it didn''t score higher but it could also be the neatimage, IMO. In any case it was a good entry. What I especially liked about this was the lighting and also the texture. The image also has a good tonal range and the whites and blacks are perfect. All in all a very good technical image that met the challenge.', '2006-06-23 04:16:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2544019, 347589, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2</b> <br/> <br/>Looking at the color version I definitely like that one better for the fabrics but overall I like the duotone version better because it takes a busy scene and keeps the focus squarely where you want it (i.e. your faces). With the color version my eyes drift all over the image too much and everything becomes a distraction. However, with that said I think the color version may have worked better with DPC voters who crave that. <br/> <br/>Well that''s it. I wish I had some real critiques here but I like this image. I think the technicals are great. I love the lighting and the composition and the layout. It''s also very sharp and it has good tonal range and lots of detail which I love. I think you did a bang up job here. I certainly can feel that moment you captured and the duotone helps to convey that.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-23 03:52:58.</i></td>', 'Greetings from CTP2  Looking at the color version I definitely like that one better for the fabrics but overall I like the duotone version better because it takes a busy scene and keeps the focus squarely where you want it (i.e. your faces). With the color version my eyes drift all over the image too much and everything becomes a distraction. However, with that said I think the color version may have worked better with DPC voters who crave that.  Well that''s it. I wish I had some real critiques here but I like this image. I think the technicals are great. I love the lighting and the composition and the layout. It''s also very sharp and it has good tonal range and lots of detail which I love. I think you did a bang up job here. I certainly can feel that moment you captured and the duotone helps to convey that.', '2006-06-23 04:50:41.000000', '2006-06-23 04:52:58.000000', 0),
