(2551146, 346125, 31794, '<td valign="top">[[trading post]]<br/> <br/>nice setup, not a very good image though, but I think you knew that and were just fishing for comments.<br/> <br/>every newyear we burn fireworks for over $ 20.000.000 in Iceland, thousands of tourist come to Iceland just before newyear to experience this show that everyone takes a part in and lasts for about 5 hours.<br/> <br/>your setup would cost at least $1000 here, as fireworks are sold by rescue squads to support their work.<br/> <br/>hope you have fun burning all of them :)</td>', '[[trading post]] nice setup, not a very good image though, but I think you knew that and were just fishing for comments. every newyear we burn fireworks for over $ 20.000.000 in Iceland, thousands of tourist come to Iceland just before newyear to experience this show that everyone takes a part in and lasts for about 5 hours. your setup would cost at least $1000 here, as fireworks are sold by rescue squads to support their work. hope you have fun burning all of them :)', '2006-06-25 09:52:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2552304, 345216, 49326, '<td valign="top">This one was one of my favorites.</td>', 'This one was one of my favorites.', '2006-06-25 18:34:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2552697, 345377, 47933, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club Judi!<br/> <br/>Well, I really don''t know what I''m supposed to say here. Your top ten finish really says a lot :D<br/> <br/>The composition is great. The wide depth of field is what this shot needed and you pulled it off nicely. The blurred foreground tree is a bit distracting. The ones off to the right really don''t come into play for me so their blur doesn''t really bother here. <br/> <br/>What would''ve made it score higher? Probably if more parents voted lol. Until a couple of weeks ago I couldn''t have understood it the way I do now. It doesn''t seem like too much of an indulgence to the average person but I think parents understand it perfectly!<br/> <br/>Overall a wonderful image!<br/> <br/>Thanks for the opportunity to critique this shot Judi.<br/> <br/>Cheers - Phil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Judi! Well, I really don''t know what I''m supposed to say here. Your top ten finish really says a lot :D The composition is great. The wide depth of field is what this shot needed and you pulled it off nicely. The blurred foreground tree is a bit distracting. The ones off to the right really don''t come into play for me so their blur doesn''t really bother here.  What would''ve made it score higher? Probably if more parents voted lol. Until a couple of weeks ago I couldn''t have understood it the way I do now. It doesn''t seem like too much of an indulgence to the average person but I think parents understand it perfectly! Overall a wonderful image! Thanks for the opportunity to critique this shot Judi. Cheers - Phil', '2006-06-25 21:49:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2552862, 346172, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment:<br/> <br/>Have to admit I didn''t even look through the Indulgence challenge.  That said, this is a sweet car - definitely fits the challenge!  I particularly like how you''ve framed the shot with the manufacturer name just above the car - that works nicely for an advertising shot for instance.  I think you''ve done a great job with the lighting as it existed in the venue - car show or dealership - whichever.  Nit (and you can''t fix it in basic) is to clone out the yellow lettering on the left.  Other than that, just a bit oversharpened - can see some jaggies along the edges of the car.</td>', 'Trading Post comment: Have to admit I didn''t even look through the Indulgence challenge.  That said, this is a sweet car - definitely fits the challenge!  I particularly like how you''ve framed the shot with the manufacturer name just above the car - that works nicely for an advertising shot for instance.  I think you''ve done a great job with the lighting as it existed in the venue - car show or dealership - whichever.  Nit (and you can''t fix it in basic) is to clone out the yellow lettering on the left.  Other than that, just a bit oversharpened - can see some jaggies along the edges of the car.', '2006-06-25 22:54:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2552882, 346125, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment:<br/> <br/>Really glad you didn''t light the sparkler... the ensuing explosions probably would have made for an interesting albeit very "blown" shot.  Definitely meets the challenge; very colorful, extremely sharp, fairly well exposed except as you noted with respect to your face.  All that said, I''d probably have given it a 6.  A good challenge entry, but you have lots better pictures.  :-)</td>', 'Trading Post comment: Really glad you didn''t light the sparkler... the ensuing explosions probably would have made for an interesting albeit very "blown" shot.  Definitely meets the challenge; very colorful, extremely sharp, fairly well exposed except as you noted with respect to your face.  All that said, I''d probably have given it a 6.  A good challenge entry, but you have lots better pictures.  :-)', '2006-06-25 22:59:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2552934, 346172, 53164, '<td valign="top">hello again,<br/> <br/>thought this was a nice shot. i liked particularly the little spots of light reflecting..... because is shows shiny but not overdone.<br/> <br/>the major problem i have is that ceiling...i know unavoidable because this is a great angle to shoot from..... but it is rather distracting.</td>', 'hello again, thought this was a nice shot. i liked particularly the little spots of light reflecting..... because is shows shiny but not overdone. the major problem i have is that ceiling...i know unavoidable because this is a great angle to shoot from..... but it is rather distracting.', '2006-06-25 23:21:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2552957, 346125, 53164, '<td valign="top">hello again,<br/> <br/>i wonder who the kid is really? lol.<br/> <br/>it is a nice shot but i thought it was a bit too much. yeah i know indulgence in and of itself is too much, but i would have liked them thrown around or messed about so there was something more in the frame. i also thought that putting yourself in, while was a great idea, was done in the wrong way..... i would have rather seen you playing with them like lighting one or something.<br/> <br/>still, it is an overall great shot nice technical performance as always. well done.</td>', 'hello again, i wonder who the kid is really? lol. it is a nice shot but i thought it was a bit too much. yeah i know indulgence in and of itself is too much, but i would have liked them thrown around or messed about so there was something more in the frame. i also thought that putting yourself in, while was a great idea, was done in the wrong way..... i would have rather seen you playing with them like lighting one or something. still, it is an overall great shot nice technical performance as always. well done.', '2006-06-25 23:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2552994, 346172, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - The car itself looks pretty cool. I like the starbursts on the various parts of the car. What is a shame is the background people, cars and ceiling. Really draws away from your subject. In an ideal world you could have asked to take it outside for a spin to get a proper picture with oen of your icelandic backgrounds - that would be ribbon all the way.</td>', 'Trading Post - The car itself looks pretty cool. I like the starbursts on the various parts of the car. What is a shame is the background people, cars and ceiling. Really draws away from your subject. In an ideal world you could have asked to take it outside for a spin to get a proper picture with oen of your icelandic backgrounds - that would be ribbon all the way.', '2006-06-25 23:31:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2553327, 344790, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>Well you can''t get more indulgent than that for the common man. :P As coronamv pointed out in his comment, a thicker head would have bumped up the appeal. Also, the focus is off a bit. The lower bubbles are fairly sharp but you are not using a wide enough depth of field. I would bump up the aperture setting to at least F/8 to get more of that rim in focus. <br/> <br/>Another thing to consider is shooting at a slightly lower angle so that we don''t see the back of the rim at all. That''s how you''ll see a lot of glass images taken when shot head on like this. <br/> <br/>That''s pretty much it. I do like the use of negative space here and how you got the glass fading into the background. Really if you just improved the DOF so that more is sharp you would have a higher scoring image.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   Well you can''t get more indulgent than that for the common man. :P As coronamv pointed out in his comment, a thicker head would have bumped up the appeal. Also, the focus is off a bit. The lower bubbles are fairly sharp but you are not using a wide enough depth of field. I would bump up the aperture setting to at least F/8 to get more of that rim in focus.  Another thing to consider is shooting at a slightly lower angle so that we don''t see the back of the rim at all. That''s how you''ll see a lot of glass images taken when shot head on like this.  That''s pretty much it. I do like the use of negative space here and how you got the glass fading into the background. Really if you just improved the DOF so that more is sharp you would have a higher scoring image.', '2006-06-26 00:36:57.000000', NULL, 0),
