(2566396, 347522, 38496, '<td valign="top">I like this!  Nice compostion, definately sitting by the pool for a pedicure would rate as an indulgence in my book!  I love the reflections of the clouds in the water.  The only ''off'' thing is that your ankle looks a little distorted, or soft or something.  Great shot, though!  I agree... should have scored higher.</td>', 'I like this!  Nice compostion, definately sitting by the pool for a pedicure would rate as an indulgence in my book!  I love the reflections of the clouds in the water.  The only ''off'' thing is that your ankle looks a little distorted, or soft or something.  Great shot, though!  I agree... should have scored higher.', '2006-06-29 14:16:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2570255, 346125, 48739, '<td valign="top">I''m In heaven(as i faint and pass out)</td>', 'I''m In heaven(as i faint and pass out)', '2006-06-30 17:58:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574289, 346172, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading Post<br/> <br/>The car is fabulous! The background however does it no justice and draws my eye away from the car.  It does seem like the car has been over-sharpened a bit as I am getting a halo effect on my monitor.  Everything about this car is low curves and horizontal flow - except the shadow of the mirror, which tends to cut the car in two pieces.  I realize that you couldn''t do anything about the lighting, but it''s a shame nonetheless.</td>', 'Trading Post The car is fabulous! The background however does it no justice and draws my eye away from the car.  It does seem like the car has been over-sharpened a bit as I am getting a halo effect on my monitor.  Everything about this car is low curves and horizontal flow - except the shadow of the mirror, which tends to cut the car in two pieces.  I realize that you couldn''t do anything about the lighting, but it''s a shame nonetheless.', '2006-07-02 07:34:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574306, 346125, 37858, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid this one doesn''t do too much for me.  While it is appropriate for the idea of "indulgence" all of the packages are just too busy for my taste.  Colors are good.  Focus is fine.  Not much more I can say.  I would have scored it a 5 had I been in town.</td>', 'I''m afraid this one doesn''t do too much for me.  While it is appropriate for the idea of "indulgence" all of the packages are just too busy for my taste.  Colors are good.  Focus is fine.  Not much more I can say.  I would have scored it a 5 had I been in town.', '2006-07-02 08:16:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2576034, 347545, 27763, '<td valign="top">I can''t believe this won a ribbon.  It''s well composed (nice tight crop), well exposed, sharp, and definitely meets the challenge, but it''s just kind of ugly, IMO.  Not ribbon material, in my book. Sorry... just my opinion. Obviously the voters/commenters disagree with me.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-03 11:01:00.</i></td>', 'I can''t believe this won a ribbon.  It''s well composed (nice tight crop), well exposed, sharp, and definitely meets the challenge, but it''s just kind of ugly, IMO.  Not ribbon material, in my book. Sorry... just my opinion. Obviously the voters/commenters disagree with me.', '2006-07-03 00:00:54.000000', '2006-07-03 12:01:00.000000', 0),
(2576065, 347589, 27763, '<td valign="top">Well done, Shailesh.</td>', 'Well done, Shailesh.', '2006-07-03 00:06:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2586065, 345444, 50641, '<td valign="top">I wrote a comment for this during the challenge but the system didn''t save it.  Really enjoyed this shot, gave it a 10 for originality and bizarreness.  The only thing that would have improved it for me would be to have kept the lights around the puppet lower so that he is spookier and his puppetness is more ambiguous.  Did that cigar come with the puppet or is that an additional prop?  Looks really lit, just like him ;-)</td>', 'I wrote a comment for this during the challenge but the system didn''t save it.  Really enjoyed this shot, gave it a 10 for originality and bizarreness.  The only thing that would have improved it for me would be to have kept the lights around the puppet lower so that he is spookier and his puppetness is more ambiguous.  Did that cigar come with the puppet or is that an additional prop?  Looks really lit, just like him ;-)', '2006-07-05 02:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2589654, 347330, 22975, '<td valign="top">i love the tones on this one.  i like subtle photos like this one.  :)</td>', 'i love the tones on this one.  i like subtle photos like this one.  :)', '2006-07-05 19:26:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2595733, 346738, 22975, '<td valign="top">very nice still life with great lighting.  i''m jealous, i can''t ever get my lighting right.  :)  fantastic capture!</td>', 'very nice still life with great lighting.  i''m jealous, i can''t ever get my lighting right.  :)  fantastic capture!', '2006-07-07 01:21:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2601298, 346172, 14414, '<td valign="top">Sorry to be late on comments<br/> <br/>This is a very clean, professional looking shot, and fits the challenge fine. I like the alignment of th word Porsche in the b/g, and the wide angle used. What bugs me, however, is the red on the wheels  - I''m assuming they''re only that colour from reflections..?<br/>It does seem a touch oversharpened, as others have pointed out. <br/>I think its a very good photo, say, for a magazine (though maybe with a slightly less busy b/g), but I can''t imagine it doing much higer than a 5.5 here, just because it doesn''t have so much life to it</td>', 'Sorry to be late on comments This is a very clean, professional looking shot, and fits the challenge fine. I like the alignment of th word Porsche in the b/g, and the wide angle used. What bugs me, however, is the red on the wheels  - I''m assuming they''re only that colour from reflections..?It does seem a touch oversharpened, as others have pointed out. I think its a very good photo, say, for a magazine (though maybe with a slightly less busy b/g), but I can''t imagine it doing much higer than a 5.5 here, just because it doesn''t have so much life to it', '2006-07-08 19:43:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2603402, 346125, 14414, '<td valign="top">Really sorry for how late these critiques are...<br/> <br/>I like the composition, with the nicely busy fireworks and the simple head centred horizontally. However, I''d prefer more black empty space around the face, which gets lost. <br/>Other than this, I do like the picture - it''s not your best but it has a nice quirkiness to it and very well suited to the challenge.</td>', 'Really sorry for how late these critiques are... I like the composition, with the nicely busy fireworks and the simple head centred horizontally. However, I''d prefer more black empty space around the face, which gets lost. Other than this, I do like the picture - it''s not your best but it has a nice quirkiness to it and very well suited to the challenge.', '2006-07-09 16:26:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2620808, 347589, 49202, '<td valign="top">Hey, Shailesh. This is a rather cute moment you shot. When critiquing duotones, however, I tend to look for high contrasts, which, unfortunately, this one doesn''t have.<br/>Which isn''t to say you this isn''t a great photo. It is, actually. Compositionallt and tonally (sic). Selective desat would''ve worked better here, though.<br/>Whatever man, congrats on the high finish. You did a great job here.</td>', 'Hey, Shailesh. This is a rather cute moment you shot. When critiquing duotones, however, I tend to look for high contrasts, which, unfortunately, this one doesn''t have.Which isn''t to say you this isn''t a great photo. It is, actually. Compositionallt and tonally (sic). Selective desat would''ve worked better here, though.Whatever man, congrats on the high finish. You did a great job here.', '2006-07-13 23:59:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2622950, 345454, 52215, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all of your comments<br/>First of all, i don''t like this pic because simply it is taken in hurry in very low light and i used my flash, but as you all seen, it is not good enough.<br/>I forgot to say that i took this shot with my 70-200L IS lens (by mistake i mentioned 24-70L).<br/>I wish to get better camera and better lens for birds like 100-400L or 500L but later i will buy more gears.<br/>I am not good in photoshop, so if someone can help me in Edit processing then i will be glad to take alot of photos nd upload RAW original photos if that possible.<br/>About the place i posted this photos i didn''t know what "indulgent" means just i saw it is an exclusive challenge which is open for all users i posted it there, i don''t have chance to take photos as challenge titles need but i want to post many photos here without enter challenge, just for critique but not in a thread i want it same as many photos here with information and comments down of the photos, of you know a way to post as many photos here free then it will be great as i am registered on another forum with better critique and free posting photos for all members and users, not making separate between members and non members.</td>', 'Thank you for all of your commentsFirst of all, i don''t like this pic because simply it is taken in hurry in very low light and i used my flash, but as you all seen, it is not good enough.I forgot to say that i took this shot with my 70-200L IS lens (by mistake i mentioned 24-70L).I wish to get better camera and better lens for birds like 100-400L or 500L but later i will buy more gears.I am not good in photoshop, so if someone can help me in Edit processing then i will be glad to take alot of photos nd upload RAW original photos if that possible.About the place i posted this photos i didn''t know what "indulgent" means just i saw it is an exclusive challenge which is open for all users i posted it there, i don''t have chance to take photos as challenge titles need but i want to post many photos here without enter challenge, just for critique but not in a thread i want it same as many photos here with information and comments down of the photos, of you know a way to post as many photos here free then it will be great as i am registered on another forum with better critique and free posting photos for all members and users, not making separate between members and non members.', '2006-07-14 18:05:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2626573, 347366, 22689, '<td valign="top">Congrats for your personal best place ! <br/></td>', 'Congrats for your personal best place ! ', '2006-07-16 11:25:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669958, 345715, 42957, '<td valign="top">I as ticked off more at my blindness for not noticing the weird cubic thing going on in the clouds than getting DQ''d...again.  Hah.  Rebel.  <br/> <br/>The halo aroud the couple was intentional.  Ish.  As for the weird cubism thing, something went wonky in the resizing or saving for web or filtering.  One of those.  I probably didn''t notice it because I looked at it too long; it was one of those things where you look at something until you don''t see it at all.<br/> <br/>This would have done all right if not for technicalities. Oh well.  There''s a better version on my deviantart account.</td>', 'I as ticked off more at my blindness for not noticing the weird cubic thing going on in the clouds than getting DQ''d...again.  Hah.  Rebel.   The halo aroud the couple was intentional.  Ish.  As for the weird cubism thing, something went wonky in the resizing or saving for web or filtering.  One of those.  I probably didn''t notice it because I looked at it too long; it was one of those things where you look at something until you don''t see it at all. This would have done all right if not for technicalities. Oh well.  There''s a better version on my deviantart account.', '2006-07-28 00:27:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2670920, 346790, 52115, '<td valign="top">Regarding HotShot7''s question below, "What''s the name of the band"<br/>It''s not that out of focus, if you look closely, you will find at least 14 places that say "Good Charlotte". That may be a definite clue.<br/> <br/>I would have included more of the ceiling and not the object in the bottom-left corner. With my luck I probably would have made it more blurry or too much contrast. If you didn''t use a tripod, maybe that would help.<br/> <br/>Tip: For very low angle shots use a home made sand-bag or bean-bag or bag of oats, instead of a tripod you could use a bag on a stepladder, pogo-stick (monopod), roof of you car, anything stationary. That allows for a greater variety of shots, varying exposure/aperture/lighting/DOF.<br/> <br/>I just thought of the "sandbag" last tuesday shooting a sunset on rocky-pier.</td>', 'Regarding HotShot7''s question below, "What''s the name of the band"It''s not that out of focus, if you look closely, you will find at least 14 places that say "Good Charlotte". That may be a definite clue. I would have included more of the ceiling and not the object in the bottom-left corner. With my luck I probably would have made it more blurry or too much contrast. If you didn''t use a tripod, maybe that would help. Tip: For very low angle shots use a home made sand-bag or bean-bag or bag of oats, instead of a tripod you could use a bag on a stepladder, pogo-stick (monopod), roof of you car, anything stationary. That allows for a greater variety of shots, varying exposure/aperture/lighting/DOF. I just thought of the "sandbag" last tuesday shooting a sunset on rocky-pier.', '2006-07-28 10:17:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2671568, 345826, 60862, '<td valign="top">This is very, very creative. :)</td>', 'This is very, very creative. :)', '2006-07-28 14:44:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2674937, 346807, 24981, '<td valign="top">HI Kelly, I see how much of an improvement you''ve made to this from the original. Well done! It''s a marked improvement over the original, for sure.<br/> <br/>I completely get the idea of using games for the challenge (one of my favorite indulgences as well!), so it fits the challenge well, imo.<br/> <br/>A couple of thoughts for you... the lighting on the CD doesn''t seem to fit well with the background. Either add more light as it sits or tilt the cd back towards the background and light it so it blends better.<br/> <br/>The CD is also noisy and I can''t tell if despeckle did what you wanted it to do. I believe Noise Ninja or Neat Image are free programs (or have a free version) and I''ve heard both work well for reducing noise. (I use NI.)<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, there are a bunch of people here who voted 1 and 2, neither of which I agree with because it''s a better photo than that. 1''s and 2''s should only be given out to images that are horrible, of which, again, this is not.<br/> <br/>Another thing I''d like to mention is your title. I love good titles. In this case, the title doesn''t convey much emotion which could have helped sway some of the voters to a point or two higher than they voted. I''m thinking of something like, "I Sold My Soul..." or "My Passion, My Soul..."<br/> <br/>That''s about all I can think of. Thanks for reading it all and if you want to discuss anything, feel free to pm me.<br/> <br/>George</td>', 'HI Kelly, I see how much of an improvement you''ve made to this from the original. Well done! It''s a marked improvement over the original, for sure. I completely get the idea of using games for the challenge (one of my favorite indulgences as well!), so it fits the challenge well, imo. A couple of thoughts for you... the lighting on the CD doesn''t seem to fit well with the background. Either add more light as it sits or tilt the cd back towards the background and light it so it blends better. The CD is also noisy and I can''t tell if despeckle did what you wanted it to do. I believe Noise Ninja or Neat Image are free programs (or have a free version) and I''ve heard both work well for reducing noise. (I use NI.) Unfortunately, there are a bunch of people here who voted 1 and 2, neither of which I agree with because it''s a better photo than that. 1''s and 2''s should only be given out to images that are horrible, of which, again, this is not. Another thing I''d like to mention is your title. I love good titles. In this case, the title doesn''t convey much emotion which could have helped sway some of the voters to a point or two higher than they voted. I''m thinking of something like, "I Sold My Soul..." or "My Passion, My Soul..." That''s about all I can think of. Thanks for reading it all and if you want to discuss anything, feel free to pm me. George', '2006-07-29 22:13:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2678519, 346562, 21816, '<td valign="top">This is great work Becky. One you should be proud of! Well done!</td>', 'This is great work Becky. One you should be proud of! Well done!', '2006-07-31 04:49:03.000000', NULL, 0),
